10, "template_override": 1}, {"type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}]}, {"type": "audio", "_data": [], "title": "", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "engenn8le11ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "Maria was woken up by the fluorescent lights of the hospital room. She'd been admitted to the hospital the day before, to undergo surgery on her knee. But now, there was a terrible pain in her stomach, and Maria just didn't feel like herself.\nJust as she was beginning to become more aware of her surroundings, a nurse bustled into the room.<br/>\nShe was greeted by the nurse. \"Ah, Mrs. Green, I see you're awake!\"  she said.<br/>\nHer voice was shaking as she said \"Mrs. Green? I'm not Mrs. Green ...\".", "image": "engenn8le11ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"text": "\"Yes, you are,\" the nurse said. \"It's here on your chart. Isabella Green, gallbladder operation. You must be confused from the anesthetic.\u201d<br/> When the nurse left, Maria looked down at her stomach and saw the stitches across her belly. But, this was not her stomach. Maria touched her face. \"This is the face and body of an old woman.\" Maria thought, as she felt the panic rise in her chest.\nShe had noticed an old man in the room who was cleaning the floor. <br/>\"What's wrong?\" the man asked.", "image": "engenn8le11ob01re2img02.jpg", "time": "30000", "id": 2}, {"text": "\"This is not me. I'm a young woman, not an old lady. I had come in yesterday for surgery and woke up like, like...\" <br/>\nThe old man looked at her wisely. \"I have a powder I keep with me for emergencies like these. When it is mixed with water, it becomes a potion. When you wake up, you'll be back to yourself.\"<br/>She thanked him and drank it down. <br/>\nTo be continued ...", "image": "engenn8le11ob01re2img03.jpg", "time": "58000", "id": 3}], "coverimg": "engenn8le11ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le11ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"type": "static", "_data": [], "title": "", "template_override": 1, "id": 2, "contents": [{"value": "<span class=\"strong\">Doctor</span>: How are you doing, dear? Are you feeling any better?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Girl</span>: I don't think so! I haven't felt the effect of the medicine yet.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Doctor</span>: What medicine? I knew you were not feeling like yourself. I'll be back in a minute.", "type": "p"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories From the Hospital", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I'm Not Mrs. Green!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject. <br/>You use a passive structure when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = When you (subject) mix the powder (object) with water, it becomes a potion.<br/> Passive sentence = When the powder (subject)  <span class=\"strong\">is mixed</span> with water, it becomes a potion. <br/><br/>  It is not necessary to mention the object from an active sentence when it is changed to a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle.<br/><br/>   The Simple Present passive form is:<br/><br/>  am/are/is + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Patients <span class=\"strong\">are greeted</span> when they wake up from surgery.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past passive form is:<br/><br/>  was/were + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Mar\u00eda <span class=\"strong\">was woken up</span> by the fluorescent lights of the hospital room.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She was greeted by the nurse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When it is mixed with water, it becomes a potion.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Past Perfect, Simple Past and Past Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an \u2018earlier past'.<br/> You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about an action that was happening at a time before now.<br/> You use the Simple Past to talk about a finished action that happened at a specific time in the past. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect</span> tense.<br/><br/>  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br/><br/>  Subject + had + past participle<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">When I arrived at the party, Vanessa <span class=\"strong\">had</span> already <span class=\"strong\">gone</span> home. </span><br/> Which event happened first? Vanessa went home.<br/> Which event happened later? I arrived at the party.<br/><br/>You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She'd been admitted to the hospital the day before.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She had noticed an old man in the room who was cleaning the floor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had come in yesterday for surgery and woke up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Continuous</span> to:<br/><br/>  <ul><li>describe the background in a story written in the past tense</li></ul> <br/>  For example:<br/>   <span class=\"italic\">The children <span class=\"strong\">were laughing</span> and the birds <span class=\"strong\">were singing</span> in the park. A woman <span class=\"strong\">was looking</span> for her phone, which she dropped somewhere ...</span><br/><br/>  <ul><li>to describe an action that was interrupted by another event or action in the past</li></ul> <br/>    For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">was reading</span> the news the other day <span class=\"strong\">when</span> I <span class=\"strong\">came across</span> an article that talked about a trial by judge.</span><br/><br/>  The form of the Past Continuous is: <br/><br/> Subject + was/were + verb-ing", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Just as she was beginning to become more aware of her surroundings, a nurse bustled into the room.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Mar\u00eda touched her face.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She thanked him and drank it down.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fluorescent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "bright and glowing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mar\u00eda was woken up by the fluorescent lights of the hospital room.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about strange events.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to undergo", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to experience something that is unpleasant or involves a change", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She'd been admitted to the hospital the day before, to undergo surgery on her knee. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to feel like yourself", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel in good health or temper as usual", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  There was a terrible pain in her stomach, and Mar\u00eda just didn't feel like herself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "surrounding", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the area and things around you", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was beginning to become more aware of her surroundings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bustle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move or behave looking busy or in a hurry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A nurse bustled into the room.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gall bladder", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an organ in the body that stores bile", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's here on your chart. Isabella Green, gall bladder operation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "anesthetic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a drug that blocks the pain someone is feeling", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must be confused from the anesthetic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stitches", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a kind of thread used to keep an open wound closed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mar\u00eda looked down at her stomach and saw the stitches across her belly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "panic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sudden feeling of being nervous and frightened", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mar\u00eda felt the panic rise in her chest when she saw the face of an old woman.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "potion", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a drink that is supposed to have magic properties, good or bad", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When it is mixed with water, it becomes a potion.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob01aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Tell a friend about a visit to the hospital in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe the events and explain how you felt about it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a description of 100 words explaining what happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the passive, past perfect and past continuous to tell the story.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your story in a group and correct any errors.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I tell a friend about a hospital visit in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a 100-word description about a hospital visit in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use passive form, past perfect, simple past and past continuous.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my story aloud and correct any errors I find.", "type": "text"}]}]}